<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "A reaction is an answer to a message that costs one click. It reaches the person who wrote the line, and it never asks anybody to read anything."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_control}>{dgettext("help_features", "How to React")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_features",
      "On a computer: hover a message and pick one of the emoji that appear under it"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_features",
      "On a phone: press and hold the message and choose React, then pick any emoji"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_features", "Click your own reaction again to take it back")}</li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_features", "What the Numbers Mean")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "The number beside an emoji is how many people chose it, and hovering it names them. Your own reactions are drawn pressed. One person counts once per emoji, however many times they click."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_mute}>{dgettext("help_features", "It Notifies Nobody")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_features",
    "A reaction plays no sound, marks nothing unread and wakes no device. That is deliberate: the cheapest thing you can say here should stay cheap for the person receiving it too."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_features", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="feature-emoji">
    {dgettext("help_features", "Emoji Picker")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-context-menus">
    {dgettext("help_features", "Context Menus")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
